{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/cli/dataset_utilities.py::validate_cohort_ids", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C6.S2", "lines": [1750, 1752, 1754, 1758], "why": "`id_list = reduce(lambda_for_list_conv, ids, [])` uses lambdas such as `a+[int(b)]`. Each step allocates a new list and copies the whole accumulator `a`, so building an n-element list copies about n squared over 2 pointers. The accumulator could be appended in place, or the list built with one comprehension. C7.S1 (quadratic algorithm) describes the same cost, and I chose C6.S2 because the waste is the repeated copy. The returned `lambda_for_list_conv` is reused in generate_pheno_filter in dx_extract_utils/cohort_filter_payload.py (lines 37 and 39), where the same quadratic build runs again. The constant is small, so this only matters for ID lists in the thousands or more. Not timed."}]}
{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/cli/dataset_utilities.py::extract_assay_expression", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C8.S4", "lines": [1468, 1475, 1571, 1578, 1664], "why": "The Dataset property `assays_info_dict` (bindings/apollo/dataset.py, line 90) is uncached and calls the uncached property `descriptor_file_dict` (line 41) on every access. That property downloads the whole descriptor with DXFile.read(), gunzips it and runs json.loads. On the default path, with no --assay-name, the function triggers seven full descriptor downloads. Line 1475 reads `dataset.assays_info_dict` twice, line 1571 reads it once, line 1578 reads it once through `assay_info_dict()`, and line 1664 reads it twice through `assay_names_list()` (dataset.py lines 121-122). With --assay-name, line 1468 adds two more through is_assay_name_valid, and the path makes five downloads in total. One download bound to a local would serve all of these, so six of the seven default-path downloads are repeats. I read dataset.py only to confirm this property behaviour."}, {"label": "b", "root_cause": "C1.S1", "lines": [1662], "why": "`DATASET_DESCRIPTOR = dataset.descriptor_file_dict` binds a value that nothing in the function reads. A search of dataset_utilities.py finds no other reference to DATASET_DESCRIPTOR. The property does a full descriptor download and parse on each read (label a), so this line alone costs one whole descriptor download per call, and removing it leaves the output unchanged."}]}
{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/cli/dataset_utilities.py::DXDatasetDictionary.create_coding_name_dframe", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C3.S4", "lines": [2292, 2293, 2294, 2295], "why": "In the flat branch, the comprehension `int(display.index(c) + 1) if c in display else None` runs once for each code. `display` is a list (`coding.get('display') or []`) holding the codes of the coding, and `c in display` and `display.index(c)` each scan it linearly. Two linear scans per code gives roughly n squared work for n codes. A dict built once with enumerate over `display` answers each lookup in constant time. C5.S2 (missing helper type) describes the same fix, and I chose C3.S4. The cost depends on the largest flat coding, which I did not measure."}]}
{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/cli/dataset_utilities.py::DXDatasetDictionary.load_data_dictionary", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C1.S5", "lines": [2068, 2069, 2070], "why": "`source_eblock = source_eblock.assign(relationship=rel, referenced_entity_field=ref)` makes a full copy of the entity data frame once per edge. The result is bound to the local `source_eblock`, which is never read again, and is not stored back into `eblocks`. Whether the writes at lines 2063-2066 reach the frame depends on how pandas returns `.values` for these columns, which I did not check. The `.assign` result is unused in either case, so the copy is wasted work. Not executed."}]}

NOTES:
Every unit in the four files was read in full. The 208 generated wrappers in api.py are one-line forwards to DXHTTPRequest, and I did not report them, because one extra frame costs little against an HTTP round trip. I checked the mutable `input_params={}` defaults. Nonce.update_nonce copies its input in the run and new wrappers, and DXHTTPRequest only serializes its data argument, so nothing accumulates across calls.
The findings in search.py and dataset_utilities.py were traced by reading. No code was run and no files were changed.
bindings/apollo/dataset.py belongs to another group. I read its property bodies only to confirm the C8.S4 finding in extract_assay_expression.
Considered and dropped as too small to report, all in dataset_utilities.py. The set(additional_fields) rebuilt inside the comprehension at lines 1645-1647 is loop-invariant but has a small N. The dead filter_arg at line 588 costs one string concatenation per call. The list() copies at lines 743-744 act on short lists. The open() without a with block in csv_from_json at lines 1183 and 1201-1202 releases on the normal path and by refcount on error.
bindings/__init__.py produced no finding. The polling loops in _wait_on_close and _wait_until_parts_uploaded are needed and back off.
The reference cards under reference/root-causes/ were not opened, as instructed.

