FILES_READ:
src/python/dxpy/utils/resolver.py: 47 units
src/python/dxpy/utils/describe.py: 48 units
src/python/dxpy/app_builder.py: 18 units
src/python/dxpy/workflow_builder.py: 28 units
src/python/dxpy/scripts/dx_build_app.py: 24 units

SUSPICIONS:
{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/app_builder.py::upload_resources", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C1.S5", "lines": [319, 336, 399, 417, 419, 429], "why": "tar_fh.add(...) at lines 336 and 399 writes every file under resources_dir into the temporary tar during the os.walk loop. The checksum lookup at 417-419 then runs, and when find_one_data_object returns an existing bundle (429-434) the whole tar is discarded. The checksum uses only names, modes and mtimes (lines 331, 393), so a metadata-only pass could decide reuse before any file content is read."}, {"label": "b", "root_cause": "C6.S2", "lines": [441, 446, 447, 448, 450], "why": "The uncompressed tar is written to tar_tmp_fh, read back in io.DEFAULT_BUFFER_SIZE chunks (447-451), and pushed through a GzipFile into a second temporary file (441, 446). The bundle bytes are written twice and read once more. tarfile.open with mode 'w:gz' would stream the compressed archive in one pass."}]}
{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/workflow_builder.py::_assert_executable_regions_match", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C8.S4", "lines": [387, 391, 392, 398, 412], "why": "The sorted list 'executables' at 387 keeps one entry per stage, so an executable used in several stages is visited several times. Each visit issues fresh remote reads: DXApplet(exect).project and DXProject(applet_project).region (391-392) and dxpy.api.app_describe(exect) (398). The handler __getattr__ calls describe when _desc is empty (bindings/__init__.py lines 99-102), so every new handler costs a request. The nested workflow_describe at 412 repeats the same way. A dict keyed by executable ID, filled once, removes the repeats."}]}
{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/scripts/dx_build_app.py::_check_file_syntax", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C1.S5", "lines": [284, 286, 289], "why": "py_compile.compile(filename, cfile=pyc_path, doraise=True) at 286 writes a bytecode file that the finally block deletes at 289 without ever reading it. Only the parse verdict is used. compile(source, filename, 'exec') in memory would give the same verdict with no file write and no unlink, provided the py_compile.PyCompileError handling at 335-342 is remapped to SyntaxError."}]}
{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/scripts/dx_build_app.py::_check_suggestions", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C8.S4", "lines": [110, 140], "why": "dxpy.api.project_describe(suggestion['project'], {'permissions': True}) at 110 runs once per suggestion. The answer depends only on the project ID, so every suggestion naming the same project repeats the request. The same pattern repeats at 140 for the nested dnanexus_link project. One lookup per distinct project ID would serve all of them."}, {"label": "b", "root_cause": "C9.S2", "lines": [126, 148], "why": "dnanexus_link = dxpy.describe(...) at 126 and 148 binds a full describe result that is never read. The call is needed for its 404 check, but the payload is discarded because only existence matters. dxpy.describe accepts a fields keyword (bindings/dxdataobject_functions.py, docstring around lines 185-190), so a restricted request could keep the check and drop the unused data."}]}
{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/scripts/dx_build_app.py::build_and_upload_locally", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C8.S4", "lines": [793, 794, 845, 846], "why": "Inside the destination_override branch, project_describe(working_project, fields region)['region'] runs at 793-794. Then, for mode == 'applet', project_describe(dest_project, same fields) runs again at 845-846. dest_project is working_project (set at 843), so the second call repeats the first with the same field and writes the same region into projects_by_region. The first result could be reused."}, {"label": "b", "root_cause": "C8.S2", "lines": [887, 888], "why": "upload_resources is called once per region inside the loop at 887-888. Each call walks resources/, builds the tar, gzips it, and computes the checksum. For an app enabled in N regions, the same resources directory is archived N times with identical content. Archiving once per run and reusing the bytes for each region would remove N-1 passes, but this needs a refactor because upload_resources bundles archiving and upload together."}]}
{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/utils/describe.py::get_resolved_jbors", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C8.S4", "lines": [296, 297], "why": "job_describe(get_job_from_jbor(orig_thing)) at 297 runs for each JBOR whose jbor_str is absent from resolved_jbors (checked at 294). jbor_to_str (line 219) includes the field name and index in the key, so two outputs of the same job with different fields miss the cache and each trigger a full job describe of the same job. print_execution_desc calls this once per changed input (describe.py lines 891-893). Caching the job description by job ID would serve every field."}]}
{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/utils/resolver.py::resolve_path", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C1.S4", "lines": [483], "why": "The expression xattr(path)['project'] + ':' + xattr(path)['id'] calls xattr(path) twice in one statement. Each call re-reads the extended attributes of the same path. One local, such as attrs = xattr(path), would serve both reads. The line only runs when _DX_FUSE is set in the environment."}]}
{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/utils/resolver.py::resolve_job_ref", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C9.S1", "lines": [602, 603], "why": "The list comprehension at 602-603 issues one DXHTTPRequest to /<id>/describe per element of the job output array, each a separate round trip. dxpy.describe accepts a list and sends one system/describeDataObjects request (bindings/dxdataobject_functions.py, describe at line 176, list branch around lines 217-228). The describe keyword dict passed here would need to map onto that bulk call."}]}
{"unit": "src/python/dxpy/utils/resolver.py::resolve_multiple_existing_paths", "suspicions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C9.S1", "lines": [988, 989], "why": "For each path, _check_resolution_needed is called with its default describe=True. For an ID, that reaches DXHTTPRequest('/' + entity_name + '/describe') at resolver.py line 703, so each ID costs one request inside the loop. Name paths are gathered and sent in one dxpy.resolve_data_objects call at line 1012, but ID paths are not. They could be gathered the same way, using the bulk describe that dxpy.describe already provides for lists."}]}

NOTES:
Every unit in all five files was read in full, and the counts were checked against top-level, method and nested def counts.
Considered and not recorded because the cost is negligible at command-line input sizes: quadratic string slicing in get_last_pos_of_char and split_unescaped (resolver.py 253-265, 309-321), parse_input_keyval splitting the whole string to take element [0] (resolver.py 1365), and json.loads raising on nearly every path in _maybe_convert_stringified_dxlink (resolver.py 414-423).
Not recorded because the effect is bounded or the case is about correctness: mutable default arguments in create_app_multi_region and _create_app (inherited_metadata={}, mutated at app_builder.py line 783 and 785) and in resolve_job_ref (describe={}, mutated at resolver.py 572).
Not recorded because I could not decide whether a refactor is possible from this repo: check_folder_exists (resolver.py 1112-1123) fetches the full subfolder list for one membership test. I could not confirm from the repo whether the API supports filtering by name.
Correctness problems seen while reading, outside the energy scope: workflow_builder.py line 548, dict.fromkeys(enabled_regions, {}), shares one dict across regions, so line 553 writes the same workflow ID into every region entry. describe.py line 489 calls desc.get('') where a field name was presumably intended.
The dxapp.json file is parsed about five times per build (app_builder.py 130 and 140, dx_build_app.py 171, 354 and 516). Each read is a small local file, so I did not record it.
Nothing was run and no files were changed. I did not open reference/root-causes/.

