{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/bindings/dxdatabase_functions.py::_download_dxdatabasefile", "what_it_does": "downloads a database file in one part, describing the database and hashing every chunk", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C1.S5", "lines": [180, 182], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "dxdatabase_desc is assigned from a describe call and never read; the parts list is rebuilt locally at 186. Removing the describe saves one API round trip per download. Network-bound."}, {"label": "b", "root_cause": "C1.S5", "lines": [256, 258, 260, 266], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "hasher is created and fed every chunk, but its only reader, verify_part, is commented out at 256 and 266, so the digest is never used. Removing the hashing removes a full MD5 pass over the file. Output bytes are unchanged."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/bindings/dxdatabase.py::DXDatabase.get_download_url", "what_it_does": "returns a cached download URL, checking object existence in the project before the cache test", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C8.S4", "lines": [176, 178, 179, 193], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "object_exists_in_project issues a describe before the cache check at 193, so the describe repeats on every chunk even while the URL is cached. Moving the cache test first skips the describe on cache hits. Matches dxfile.py, which keeps the check inside the cache-miss branch."}]}
