{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/bindings/dxglobalworkflow.py::DXGlobalWorkflow.get_underlying_workflow", "what_it_does": "returns a handler for the underlying workflow of a region, with a cache that is never written", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C8.S1", "lines": [215, 216, 218, 219, 226, 227], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "_workflows_by_region is read at 215 and never written in this module, so the lookup always misses and describe runs each call. Line 226 stores a handler in the wrong attribute and line 227 builds the same handler again. Writing the handler to _workflows_by_region fixes the cache. Network-bound."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/bindings/dxfile_functions.py::_download_dxfile", "what_it_does": "downloads a file part by part, hashing each part even when it has no md5 to compare against", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C1.S5", "lines": [402, 403, 409, 410, 494, 497], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "For a part without an md5 key the hasher created at 494 is fed every chunk at 497, but verify_part never compares that digest. Skipping the hasher for those parts removes the hashing. Applies only to parts without md5, which the code does not say how often occur."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/bindings/dxfile.py::DXFile._write2", "what_it_does": "buffers writes and flushes full buffers, recursing with the unsent remainder of the data each time", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C6.S2", "lines": [524, 532], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "Each buffer-full recurses with data[remaining_space:], copying everything still unsent. A write of N bytes into buffers of B bytes copies about N squared over 2B. A loop over offsets copies each byte once. The TODO at 530 names the same concern. Network-bound: write_request uploads, so the generator is expected to fail."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/bindings/dxfile.py::DXFile.__iter__", "what_it_does": "yields lines of a file read in large chunks, splitting each chunk into a full list before yielding its first line", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C6.S3", "lines": [327, 328, 330], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "parts = _buffer.split('\\n') builds a list of every line in each chunk before the first is yielded, and the list is dropped after the chunk. A generator that scans for newlines yields each line without the list. Network-bound: read() calls the server."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/bindings/mount_all_inputs.py::mount_all_inputs", "what_it_does": "mounts job inputs with dxfuse, starting subprocesses for mkdir and id", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C10.S2", "lines": [125, 152, 153], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "os.makedirs and os.getuid/os.getgid would replace the subprocesses, but subprocess mkdir raises CalledProcessError on an existing directory and makedirs raises FileExistsError. A caller that catches the first would see a different exception type, which the contract forbids."}, {"label": "b", "root_cause": "C1.S5", "lines": [161], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The find walk prints the mount tree to stdout, so its output is part of what the job log shows. Removing it changes printed output, which the contract covers."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/cli/download.py::download", "what_it_does": "downloads named paths, listing a project's folders for each path argument", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C9.S2", "lines": [228, 229], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "list_subfolders fetches the full project folder list and filters it locally to the one name that matches abs_path. list_folder(folder=parent_folder, only='folders') returns only the direct subfolders and is already used in cp.py. Network-bound."}, {"label": "b", "root_cause": "C8.S4", "lines": [190, 228], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The project folder listing is requested inside the per-path loop, so each path argument refetches it. Fetching it once per project before the loop serves all paths."}]}
