{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/app_builder.py::upload_resources", "what_it_does": "archives the resources directory, checks for an existing bundle with the same checksum, and uploads a new one if none exists", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C1.S5", "lines": [319, 336, 399, 417, 419, 429], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The whole tar is built before the checksum lookup decides reuse, and the tar is discarded when a bundle exists. The checksum depends only on names, modes and mtimes, so a metadata pass could decide reuse first. This is a restructure of the function rather than one line, so it may not reduce to a single measured repair."}, {"label": "b", "root_cause": "C6.S2", "lines": [441, 446, 447, 448, 450], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "The uncompressed tar is re-read and gzipped into a second file. A tarfile 'w:gz' stream would produce the same members but a different gzip byte stream, so the uploaded file's bytes change. The contract covers the files written."}]}
