{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/scripts/dx_build_app.py::_check_file_syntax", "what_it_does": "checks a Python file's syntax by writing a bytecode file and deleting it again", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C1.S5", "lines": [284, 286, 289], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "compile() in memory would skip the file write, but it raises SyntaxError where py_compile raises PyCompileError, so the exception type seen by the caller changes. The contract forbids that, and mapping the error back is not a one-line repair."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/scripts/dx_build_app.py::_check_suggestions", "what_it_does": "checks the suggestions of each input, describing a project and an object for each one", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C8.S4", "lines": [110, 140], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "project_describe(suggestion['project']) runs once per suggestion, though the answer depends only on the project id. One lookup per distinct project serves all of them. Network-bound."}, {"label": "b", "root_cause": "C9.S2", "lines": [126, 148], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "dxpy.describe of a file or record binds the full result, which the code never reads; only the 404 check matters. A describe with a fields restriction keeps the check and drops the payload. Network-bound."}]}
{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/scripts/dx_build_app.py::build_and_upload_locally", "what_it_does": "builds an app locally, uploading resources to each enabled region", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C8.S4", "lines": [793, 794, 845, 846], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "project_describe(working_project, region) runs at 793-794, and the same describe runs again at 845-846 for dest_project, which is the same project. Reusing the first result removes one API call. Network-bound."}, {"label": "b", "root_cause": "C8.S2", "lines": [887, 888], "verdict": "rejected", "why": "upload_resources is called once per region and archives the directory each time. Archiving once would need upload_resources to take a prepared archive, which changes its signature and contract, so no single-unit repair exists here."}]}
