{"step": 2, "unit": "src/python/dxpy/scripts/dx.py::run_body", "what_it_does": "builds and submits a job run from the parsed inputs, describing the executable and the cloned job along the way", "decisions": [{"label": "a", "root_cause": "C6.S2", "lines": [3234], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "copy.deepcopy of the whole cloned job description runs only to read one key. Reading the key directly gives the same value, because SystemRequirementsDict already deep-copies what it keeps."}, {"label": "b", "root_cause": "C8.S4", "lines": [3272, 3375], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "The executable is described again at 3272 or 3375 although get_executable_description already described it at the top of run_body. Reusing that result removes one API call on the paths that reach these lines."}, {"label": "c", "root_cause": "C8.S4", "lines": [3389], "verdict": "accepted", "why": "dxpy.describe of each workflow stage's executable runs with no memo, so stages that share an executable describe it more than once. Moderate confidence: depends on how often stages share executables."}]}
